 "translation": "Bedi probably knows how bravely she is living, how she is staring at death with stony eyes in such a world where even her husband doesn't recognize her. Then, among them, someone repeats her name 'Suhagwanti, Suhagwali' to herself and, seeing her brother in the huge crowd, says for the last time, \"You don't recognize me either, Bihari? I fed you in my lap!\" And Bihari wanted to shout. Then he would look at his parents, and his parents, placing their hands on their hearts, would look towards Narayan Baba, and in a state of utter helplessness, Narayan Baba would look towards the sky, which in reality holds no truth and is merely an illusion of our sight, which is merely a limit beyond which our eyes cannot see.",
